h2("4.1. Detection Performance and Comparison with Baselines")
p("Table 3 reports test performance on UNSW-NB15 at the conventional threshold of 0.5 and at the validation false-alarm budget. At τ = 0.5, all models except the single-token control fall within a narrow band: F1 between 89.0% and 89.7% and ROC-AUC between 0.978 and 0.984. FTT-IDS (F1 89.45 ± 0.60%, ROC-AUC 0.9841 ± 0.0014) matches XGBoost (89.50 ± 0.04%, 0.9839) and RF (89.43 ± 0.03%, 0.9835). All models share the same failure mode at this threshold: recall is close to 99%, but roughly a quarter of the normal test traffic (24.7–28.3%) is flagged as malicious. The MSc thesis reported the same pattern for its single-seed model (accuracy 86.99%, FPR 27.6%).")
