p("**Training-set duplicates.** Table 13 compares the protocol of this study with a control in which the 67,601 duplicates are left in the training file, so that copies of a record can fall on both sides of the training–validation split. Duplicates inflate every validation estimate: validation accuracy rises by 2.3–2.4 points and validation ROC-AUC by 0.006–0.007 for all four models. Test performance does not improve; ROC-AUC is lower by 0.0004–0.0015 and the detection rate at 1% test FPR by 0.3–1.3 points, and the false-positive rates at both thresholds change by less than two points in either direction. Removing duplicates therefore does not make the models better or worse on the official test set. Its value is that the validation figures, on which every selection step relies, are not overstated.")
